      "id": 95777,
      "name": "Ameena",
      "username": "Ameena",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/{size}/1907_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-03-15T22:16:49.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>You can have some fun with something like the Scholar and the Adept, if the latter lets the former play DDA, which lets someone else do something big (Unload, for example), and once that's all done you're still in the Adept's Power phase so can do a bunch more stuff. Yay for the do-loads-of-stuff heroes :D.</p><p>One of the best games we had a few weeks ago was TLT, the Adept, and Unity, in that order. TLT let everyone draw loads of things, so I (as the Adept) got a load of stuff to set up in play and Unity had a handful of bots. I had Inventive Preparation in play within a turn or two, along with an instrument which could activate its Accompany text. As a result I was letting Unity play at least one bot on my turn, every round. I can't remember who we were fighting (Dawn, possibly), but whomever it was, they didn't last long &gt;:).</p>",
